{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consider evaluating the render assertions independently of the strict `raw == wire` check so a benign storage-normalization diff does not preempt the render verdict.","criteria":["correctness","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["`assert raw == wire, f\"Jira DC did not store the wiki wire verbatim.{diag}\"` (line 181) precedes the heading/bold/code render assertions at lines 183-191","`_rich_markdown` returns a body ending in a trailing newline: `...\\n{{code}}\\n{code}\\n{{code}}\\n` (line 72), a common target for server-side normalization","The diag string is included in every assertion message, so failure is still loud — this is a sequencing/masking concern, not a fail-open"],"finding":"In the direct-wire probe, `assert raw == wire` is evaluated before the three render assertions; if Jira DC stores the wiki source with any benign normalization (e.g. stripping the trailing newline from `_rich_markdown`'s final `\\n`), this first assertion fails and the probe never evaluates whether the body RENDERED correctly — potentially masking the very render verdict the probe exists to capture.","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py:181","norm_id":"naeb14c3d63652411","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily"